Case: API-07 (setup-code against a real, stopped, current test-owned node — the "start" branch)
Commit: e9cc21bf28e7c9435aef0ce447f35aeba5be87f8 (branch codex/docker-setup-code-wait-feedback)
Environment: same isolated environment as API-05/API-06, against the same test-owned autobyteus-server-1
node, stopped first with `docker stop autobyteus-server-1` (real Docker Desktop daemon).
Date: 2026-11-09 (~16:37 UTC)

Why this case: the implementation handoff's Known Risks records that the shared offline fake Docker always
reports State.Running=true, so start_node's "docker start" branch (a stopped-but-current node) is not
independently exercised by any fixture in this ticket's offline suite. This real-daemon case closes that
exact gap: it stops the real test node, then runs setup-code, exercising the real "start a stopped
container" branch of start_node / the real wait loop for a node that takes a moment to answer again after a
restart.

Commands:
  docker stop autobyteus-server-1   # (real Docker Desktop socket)
  env HOME="$BASE/home" SHELL=/bin/bash \
    DOCKER_HOST="unix:///Users/normy/.docker/run/docker.sock" \
    AUTOBYTEUS_DOCKER_STATE_DIR="$BASE/state" \
    AUTOBYTEUS_DOCKER_SHARED_WORKSPACE_DIR="$BASE/shared" \
    bash scripts/public/docker/autobyteus-docker.sh setup-code --name autobyteus-server-1

Exit code: 0

